  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>chi2gof</keyword>
  <short_description>Chi-square goodness-of-fit test.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>h = chi2gof(x)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>h = chi2gof(x, Name, Value)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[h, p, stats] = chi2gof(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>chi2gof</b> performs a chi-square goodness-of-fit test for a real numeric vector. Non-finite observations and nonpositive or non-finite frequencies are omitted.</p>
    <p>Name-value arguments include <b>Alpha</b>, <b>NBins</b>, <b>Ctrs</b>, <b>Edges</b>, <b>CDF</b>, <b>Expected</b>, <b>Frequency</b>, <b>NParams</b>, and <b>EMin</b>. <b>CDF</b> can be a two-column matrix or a function handle.</p>
    <p>The <b>stats</b> output contains <b>chi2stat</b>, <b>df</b>, <b>edges</b>, <b>O</b>, and <b>E</b>.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[x = norminv(((1:100) - 0.5) / 100);
[h, p, stats] = chi2gof(x)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
